4. RESTRICTIONS WORTH KNOWING
-----------------------------

  Piper is GPL-3.0-or-later.
    Piper links espeak-ng for phonemization, which is why it is copyleft. This
    repository does not ship Piper and does not link it. Piper runs as its own
    process behind an HTTP API; no file in this repository imports it; and its
    dependency is declared in a separate requirements file that
    SKIP_SPEECH=1 ./install.sh omits entirely. With speech disabled the demo
    runs silently and nothing else changes. Anyone distributing a bundle that
    includes Piper should satisfy themselves that their own arrangement meets
    the GPL's terms.

  Qualcomm QNN SDK and libqnn1 are proprietary.
    They are installed from Ubuntu's Qualcomm packages or fetched by
    ExecuTorch under Qualcomm's own license. Nothing from them is
    redistributed here, and this repository grants no rights to them.

  Llama 3.2 weights are source-available, not open source.
    See the attribution section above. Fetched at install time, never
    redistributed here.

  Neither the training images nor any trained model is published.
    A trained model is a derivative of its training data, so no .pte file is
    distributed here either. You produce model.pte and model_qnn.pte from your
    own training run. See docs/dataset.md for the provenance and consent
    position, and for the rules on collecting more images.


